+/* Vessel: the families Windows programs ask for by name, and what answers here.
+ *
+ * WHY A TABLE IN dwrite AND NOT REGISTRY ENTRIES, which is the obvious fix and
+ * does not work. `loader/wine.inf.in` registers twenty TrueType faces -- arial.ttf,
+ * tahoma.ttf, times.ttf, cour.ttf, msgothic.ttc and the rest -- and on this device
+ * `factory_create_system_fontset` rejects twenty-one files at every startup with
+ * hr 0x88985003, DWRITE_E_FILENOTFOUND. Repointing those registry values at files
+ * that exist changes nothing, because DirectWrite takes the family name from the
+ * file's own `name` table and not from the key it was filed under:
+ * Roboto-Regular.ttf registered as "Tahoma (TrueType)" still joins the collection
+ * as Roboto. The registry decides which files are read; it cannot decide what they
+ * are called.
+ *
+ * WHY NOT FontSubstitutes OR Replacements, the other obvious fix: Skia consults
+ * neither. That is the finding that made patches/wine/0057 necessary after four
+ * GDI-side font fixes had changed nothing -- Chromium goes straight to the
+ * DirectWrite collection, so the alias belongs where the collection is searched.
+ *
+ * WHAT IS NOT IN HERE, and it is the half that matters most. Wine ships real
+ * tahoma.ttf, tahomabd.ttf, symbol.ttf, webdings.ttf, wingding.ttf and marlett.ttf
+ * in its own font directory, and DirectWrite cannot see them: `create_system_path_list`
+ * resolves a bare registry name against %WINDIR%/fonts alone, while win32u's
+ * `add_system_font_resource` (win32u/font.c:6500) tries the data directory too.
+ * Those six are fixed by linking the real files into the prefix --
+ * PrefixRegistry.WINE_LINKED_FONTS -- because Wine's Tahoma *is* Tahoma, and
+ * Symbol, Wingdings, Webdings and Marlett carry dingbats no Noto face substitutes.
+ * They appear below only as the row that fires if that link failed.
+ *
+ * WHAT THIS IS NOT. It is not a substitution table in the Windows sense and does
+ * not pretend the metrics match; a program that asks for Arial and is handed
+ * Roboto gets different advance widths. That is the trade, and it is the one 0056
+ * and 0057 already made: a face with the wrong metrics is a rendered UI, and the
+ * alternative measured on this device is no UI at all. It runs only when the
+ * requested family is genuinely absent, so on a machine holding the real fonts
+ * every row below is dead code.
+ *
+ * THE THIRD INSTANCE OF ONE PATTERN. 0056 fixed GDI SystemLink chains naming five
+ * absent faces; 0057 fixed the DirectWrite fallback table naming 59 absent Noto
+ * families; this fixes family lookup itself. Every layer of Wine's font stack
+ * hardcodes Microsoft font names, and each has to be told separately what exists.
+ *
+ * Targets are best-first and every one is tried, so this survives a device with
+ * some and not others: Android guarantees Roboto, while Noto coverage varies by
+ * vendor and OS version. If no target in a row is present the lookup fails exactly
+ * as it did before. */
+struct vessel_family_alias
+{
+    const WCHAR *requested;
+    const WCHAR *targets[4];
+};
